FEX thunkgen: leave out what cannot be repacked, report errors (SteamARM)

With THUNKGEN_SKIP_UNREPACKABLE set (scripts/build-fex-thunks.sh, 32-bit
Vulkan only), a function with a pointer parameter whose pointee can be
neither passed through nor repacked is left out, named on stderr, instead of
failing the whole library; the guest then gets NULL for it from
vkGet*ProcAddr. thunkgen's own errors (std::runtime_error) are printed
instead of ending in an uncaught-exception abort without a message.

